==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-double back.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|*}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} To [[retrace]] one's steps; to go back where one has already gone.
#: ''They '''doubled back''' in hopes of finding the road again.''
#* {{quote-journal
|en
|date=July 23, 2017
|author=Brandon Nowalk
|title=The great game begins with a bang on Game Of Thrones (newbies)
|work=The Onion AV Club
|url=http://www.avclub.com/tvclub/great-game-begins-bang-game-thrones-newbies-258485
|page=
|passage=And now she has the real dilemma: press on to King’s Landing, where I have no doubt she could get as close to killing Cersei as anyone else, or '''double back''' to Winterfell to reunite with her family.}}

